WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:14.480
I gotta be honest, even though I absolutely
love emotional storytelling, it actually takes

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.820
quite a bit to make me tear up when reading
or watching something.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:24.730
The fact that this scene made be ball my eyes
out with a really weird mixture of feelings,

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:30.619
says a lot about impact that the Minks’
furiously loyal sacrifice on Zou had in the

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:32.160
story.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.149
While I would personally say that post-time
skip one piece, at least so far, has had significantly

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:44.020
fewer powerful and iconic moments than before
the time skip, this one here easily can compete

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.020
with them.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:52.199
Thus, I think it’s no wonder that we have
to talk about chapter 816 and episode 767

00:00:52.199 --> 00:00:55.899
in our the iconic scene analysis series - trademark.

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:01.239
So make yourself comfortable with some hot
coffee, grab some tissues and let’s analyse

00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.670
one of the two biggest plot twists in the
story of One Piece so far.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:10.479
Oh, yeah and if you haven’t done so already,
make sure to subscribe to the channel.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:22.330
It’s free and you get updates on any of
my future videos.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:27.340
After witnessing all the horrors that Jack,
one of the commanders of Kaido, had dealt

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.289
to the Minks and their city in his search
for Raizo - one of the main antagonists of

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:37.149
the Yonko - , Franky, Robin and Brook learn
that Kinemon and Kanjuro have already landed

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:39.880
on the island and met with Momonosuke.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:46.079
Since all the Minks have sworn under torture,
pain and death that there is no samurai Raizo

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:50.560
hidden on their island, the straw hats fear
that their arrival will trigger and enrage

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:56.159
the Minks, who apparently have suffered through
all these atrocities for some samurai that

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:04.770
they don’t even know.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.869
However the Wano samurai have already been
noticed and both Inuarashi as well as Nekomamushi,

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.900
the two rulers of the Minks, that had been
facing off with Jack, mobilise their troops

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.640
in search for them.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:22.950
At the whale forest, the remaining straw hats
together with a confused Luffy try to find

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:27.930
Kinemon and Kanjuro to keep them from encountering
any Minks.

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:31.120
Finally all four parties approach each other.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:36.060
When Nekomamushi and Inuarashi - that have
hated and avoided each other for years - meet

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:40.720
each other, the tension between the two immediately
rises.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.880
The straw hats meanwhile manage to knock Kinemon
and the others out of view before they can

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.590
get spotted, as they witness the two Mink
leaders exchanging taunts, accompanied by

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:56.620
flashbacks of their torture by the beast pirates
put up on crucifixes after Jack used one of

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:02.060
Caesar’s chemical weapons to render the
Minks paralysed and unable to fight back.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:08.040
In the heat of their argument, both Nekomamushi
and Inuarashi draw their weapons, but before

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:20.970
they can start fighting seriously, Kinemon
steps up and shouts at them to stop.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:25.830
When the minks recognise the samurai, the
straw hats expect the worse and try to convince

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.580
Kinemon to flee.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:33.659
With Momo and Kanjuro by his side he proclaims
himself as a samurai of Wano and on the look

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:36.040
for his comrade Raizo.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:42.650
At the peak of the tension, suddenly, all
of the Minks kneel down and reveal that Raizo

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:44.810
is safe.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:50.340
To the shock of the crew, the Minks explain
that the Kozuki and the Minks had a very old

00:03:50.340 --> 00:04:04.239
and deep connection and that they would never
sell out a friend, even if it meant death.

00:04:04.239 --> 00:04:05.659
Told ya guys to get some tissues.

00:04:05.659 --> 00:04:06.659
Damn.

00:04:06.659 --> 00:04:12.829
Now, there are actually a number of reasons
why this moment works so incredibly well.

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:17.750
On a basic level, the basic story beats of
the scene are actually quite similar to the

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:23.310
first video in this series: Zoro taking on
Luffy’s pain on Thriller bark.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:29.310
The focus of moth scenes lies on a fierce
display of loyalty in the face of pain and

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.110
possibly even death.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:38.310
It is the ultimate display of honour and altruism,
with no hopes or expectations of gaining anything

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.919
yourself, but a clear conscience.

00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:47.250
Just as Zoro is willing to end his own life
and dream for Luffy’s sake, the entire Mink

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:53.430
tribe is prepared to sacrifice their entire
culture and race for one single samurai.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:05:01.650
One could say that they’d be willing to
give an arm and a leg for a friend.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:07.130
Even though, this is quite ideological, it
nonetheless works perfectly.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:12.130
Because Oda has put in the necessary narrative
ground-work and foreshadowing to make both

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:17.630
moments feel absolutely natural and organic
for these characters.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:23.210
Through this moment, Oda characterises the
minks not only as a tribe of powerful fighters,

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:36.470
but also as a nation that never even thought
about betraying their allies.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.039
As we now know, there was no traitor amongst
them.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:44.750
All of them knew that Raizo was there and
they even had to restrain him to keep him

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.620
from joining the fight and being caught.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:53.250
For many chapters, Oda made us believe that
he really wasn't there and we see them being

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:59.250
tortured, poisoned and suffering for days,
for what seemed like no good reason at all

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.760
at the time.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:06.440
Surely no-one would be willing to use a limb
or even their life for some random samurai.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:12.229
And even if they did, surely at least SOME
of them would put their lives or the lives

00:06:12.229 --> 00:06:14.460
of their loved ones first.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:15.550
But no.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:22.220
They all suffered through all of it gladly,
which makes the minks not only the most loyal,

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:26.380
but also the most kind-hearted race in the
story.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:31.250
This of course becomes even more powerful
in the context of Oden and his backstory with

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:32.650
his retainers.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:38.140
His ability to inspire this level of commitment
and determination in his retainers, as well

00:06:38.140 --> 00:06:44.820
as the tragic backstory for all of them, give
this moment even more power on a re-read than

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.300
it already had in the first place.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:57.330
A truly inspirational scene.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:03.660
Now the thing that amplifies this already
powerful theme of loyalty and sacrifice even

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:09.610
more , and that differentiates it from the
Zoro moment, is the major plot twist that

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.840
Oda pulls with the reveal of Raizo’s safety.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:18.789
I personally think that throughout the first
two thirds of the Zou arc, Oda does a wonderful

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:24.750
job of creating the impression that Raizo
is really not here and that Jack is either

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:31.319
operating based on wrong information or simply
enjoys tormenting the Minks.

00:07:31.319 --> 00:07:33.350
Or maybe both.

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:37.900
The conviction with which the Minks lie and
denounce the samurai in front of the beats

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.960
pirates is portrait quite convincingly I think.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:47.380
And so the wow effect, that is wonderfully
reflected in the straw hats reaction, really

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:52.289
increases the emotional impact of the twist
significantly.

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:57.470
Seeing the likes of Zoro and Luffy, both of
whom have pulled quite similar moves before

00:07:57.470 --> 00:08:03.930
as well, genuinely shocked and moved by this,
really drives this moment home for me.

00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:09.240
In my opinion, this is actually the best plot
twist in all of One Piece, beside maybe the

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.030
reveal of CP9 on Water 7.

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:19.720
That however had less of an emotional impact
and more of a shock-reaction.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:28.099
I 
personally feel like the anime did an exceptional

00:08:28.099 --> 00:08:32.850
job with this scene, especially after the
disaster of Dressrosa.

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:38.080
In the manga, the double-spread with the minks
kneeling and Nekomamushi and Inuarashi showing

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:44.760
their relief at Kinemon's arrival really got
me and reading the chapter packed quite a

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.760
punch.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:51.730
But this is one of these moments, where music,
dialog and the visuals have the potential

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.610
to amplify the scene even more.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:09:00.230
And in this case, the animators did a great
job of representing all this I think.

00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:06.790
The original soundtrack made for this scene
in particular is just great.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:11.290
Even just hearing it outside of the scene
gives me goosebumps and you can tell that

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:18.280
it was tailored to this scene, because it
works just perfectly.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:23.650
Combined with perfectly timed silences and
the individual close ups of the straw hats

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:29.640
and the minks, it makes for a very emotional
viewing experience that actually started a

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:34.920
positive trend in regards to the anime for
me, that I had found quite disappointing during

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:43.890
previous arcs.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:49.060
And going away from the emotional impact of
the scene, Oda also integrates quite a bit

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:52.810
of world-building and characterisation into
the Raizo reveal.

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:57.960
It gives us a much completer picture of Wano
and it’s structures.

00:09:57.960 --> 00:10:04.010
For the very first time we learn about Kozuki
Oden, one of the most badass characters in

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:10.070
the entire story, that traveled together with
both Whitebeard and Roger with whom he set

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:13.210
foot on the legendary island of Laugh tale.

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:19.350
We learn of his death and of Momo’s true
identity as his heir and leader of the scabbards.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:24.870
And when we finally meet Raizo, not only do
we get to know the person who the Minks suffered

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:30.900
for, but we also learn about the existence
of the road poneglyphs as the sign posts to

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.830
Laugh tale.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:37.470
In general, the Raizo moment forms the centre
of one of my favourite arcs.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:46.090
Zou is quite short, but very powerful in terms
of both storytelling AND world building.

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:51.720
Throughout the New World, from Fishman Island
until Dressrosa, there was a bit of a lack

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:57.450
of focus on the straw hats as a crew and the
arcs were quite lengthy.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:03.770
With Zou, we get a ton of great straw hat
moments and the set-up for the next arc, that

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.820
is focused around crew-internal struggles.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:12.520
It’s short and straight to the point, but
full to the brim with information and story

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:14.260
beats.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.250
No matter how strong One Piece will undoubtedly
get in the new World until we reach Laugh

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:26.980
tale, Raizo is safe will always stay one of
the most iconic moments after the time skip.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:41.540
And to keep the ball rolling, the next iconic
moment I want to talk about is this one here.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:46.630
In my opinion Corazon’s character and his
sacrifice for Law are dramatically under-rated.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:50.610
And so we’ll be looking at that in the next
video.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:51.610
Thanks guys.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:51.950
Peace.

